1
00:00:03,320 --> 00:00:04,729
On July 8th,

2
00:00:04,779 --> 00:00:05,677
2014,

3
00:00:05,727 --> 00:00:07,574
in Belo Horizonte,

4
00:00:07,624 --> 00:00:14,140
Germany need just twenty-nine minutes to score
five goals against Brazil, at home,

5
00:00:14,190 --> 00:00:16,620
in a World Cup semi-final.

6
00:00:17,047 --> 00:00:18,049
For years,

7
00:00:18,099 --> 00:00:20,680
that match is treated as rock bottom,

8
00:00:20,730 --> 00:00:24,948
the kind of humiliation that happens
once in a lifetime and that,

9
00:00:24,998 --> 00:00:27,229
precisely because it is so big,

10
00:00:27,279 --> 00:00:30,210
should force Brazilian
football to rebuild.

11
00:00:30,260 --> 00:00:31,847
The logic is simple:

12
00:00:31,897 --> 00:00:34,420
after seven-one, the only way is up.

13
00:00:34,823 --> 00:00:36,152
Twelve years later,

14
00:00:36,202 --> 00:00:38,450
the problem is no longer a scoreline.

15
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:42,996
It is that Brazilian fans have stopped
expecting anything from their own national

16
00:00:43,046 --> 00:00:43,660
team.

17
00:00:44,083 --> 00:00:44,849
In December 2024,

18
00:00:44,899 --> 00:00:45,372
in Doha,

19
00:00:45,422 --> 00:00:47,657
Vinícius Júnior is named the best
player in the world by FIFA,

20
00:00:47,707 --> 00:00:48,898
ahead of Rodri and Bellingham,

21
00:00:48,948 --> 00:00:50,760
the first Brazilian to win it
since Kaká in 2007,

22
00:00:50,810 --> 00:00:53,568
and for one night it looks like Brazil have
finally found the heir to Romário,

23
00:00:53,618 --> 00:00:54,580
Ronaldo and Ronaldinho.

24
00:01:05,908 --> 00:01:08,073
Less than two years later,

25
00:01:08,123 --> 00:01:13,220
that same player is whistled by Real
Madrid's own fans at the Bernabéu.

26
00:01:13,653 --> 00:01:13,917
And in Brazil,

27
00:01:13,967 --> 00:01:14,332
he has become a joke.

28
00:01:14,382 --> 00:01:15,262
When he has a cosmetic procedure
on his chin this summer,

29
00:01:15,312 --> 00:01:16,221
the internet finds the perfect
explanation for his decline:

30
00:01:16,271 --> 00:01:16,936
the real Vini died on the operating table,

31
00:01:16,986 --> 00:01:17,737
and the man on the pitch
today is a body double.

32
00:01:17,787 --> 00:01:18,252
Because for a lot of people,

33
00:01:18,302 --> 00:01:19,482
that is the only way to explain how the best
player in the world got this bad,

34
00:01:19,532 --> 00:01:19,740
this fast.

35
00:01:38,612 --> 00:01:42,660
And when you watch him in a yellow shirt,
you understand why the joke stuck.

36
00:01:49,092 --> 00:01:50,302
It does not look like a
player in bad form.

37
00:01:50,352 --> 00:01:51,785
It looks like someone who does
not want to be there.

38
00:01:51,835 --> 00:01:52,971
And that is exactly what hurts the fans,

39
00:01:53,021 --> 00:01:55,096
because they remember a time when the best
player in the world wore yellow and

40
00:01:55,146 --> 00:01:56,900
played as if that shirt was the most
important thing in his life.

41
00:02:07,390 --> 00:02:11,954
So the question is no longer whether
Brazil will win the next World Cup.

42
00:02:12,004 --> 00:02:13,049
It is what,

43
00:02:13,099 --> 00:02:13,972
exactly,

44
00:02:14,022 --> 00:02:16,740
happened to the Brazilian national team.

45
00:02:21,747 --> 00:02:23,184
To understand it,

46
00:02:23,234 --> 00:02:25,028
start with the captain.

47
00:02:25,078 --> 00:02:26,337
In March 2025,

48
00:02:26,387 --> 00:02:29,490
days before facing
Argentina in Buenos Aires,

49
00:02:29,540 --> 00:02:33,237
Raphinha gives an interview to
Romário and promises to,

50
00:02:33,287 --> 00:02:34,070
quote,

51
00:02:34,120 --> 00:02:37,580
beat them up, on the pitch and
off it if necessary.

52
00:02:37,981 --> 00:02:40,534
Argentina answer by winning four-one,

53
00:02:40,584 --> 00:02:45,740
and after the final whistle their players are
filmed singing a chant aimed at him.

54
00:02:46,144 --> 00:02:46,625
Three months later,

55
00:02:46,675 --> 00:02:47,156
already on holiday,

56
00:02:47,206 --> 00:02:48,787
Raphinha talks about the Club World Cup
and says it is hard to give up your

57
00:02:48,837 --> 00:02:49,121
holidays,

58
00:02:49,171 --> 00:02:50,025
and that not everyone will want to go.

59
00:02:50,075 --> 00:02:50,694
He is talking about clubs,

60
00:02:50,744 --> 00:02:51,067
not Brazil,

61
00:02:51,117 --> 00:02:51,401
but Zico,

62
00:02:51,451 --> 00:02:52,463
who played three World Cups
and never won one,

63
00:02:52,513 --> 00:02:54,232
replies that if Raphinha had played that
tournament in the middle of his holidays,

64
00:02:54,282 --> 00:02:54,900
he would not have said it.

65
00:03:09,118 --> 00:03:09,703
And in November 2026,

66
00:03:09,753 --> 00:03:10,862
before a trip to Asia with
the national team,

67
00:03:10,912 --> 00:03:12,263
the captain says that if
Ancelotti really counts on him,

68
00:03:12,313 --> 00:03:13,269
he knows he has to manage his minutes.

69
00:03:13,319 --> 00:03:14,363
He has had three injuries in eight months,

70
00:03:14,413 --> 00:03:15,413
but in Brazil nobody hears the injuries.

71
00:03:15,463 --> 00:03:17,207
What they hear is a player choosing which
matches to play for his country.

72
00:03:17,257 --> 00:03:18,017
At the next press conference,

73
00:03:18,067 --> 00:03:19,220
when he tries to explain
himself, this happens.

74
00:03:46,384 --> 00:03:49,713
Twenty-four seconds without
finishing the sentence.

75
00:03:49,763 --> 00:03:50,801
Days later,

76
00:03:50,851 --> 00:03:54,524
he walks out against Japan
wearing the captain's armband,

77
00:03:54,574 --> 00:03:56,700
and he leaves with a red card.

78
00:03:57,133 --> 00:03:59,776
Bruno Guimarães is a different story
that ends in the same place.

79
00:03:59,826 --> 00:04:01,769
In the round of sixteen of
the 2026 World Cup,

80
00:04:01,819 --> 00:04:02,617
against Norway,

81
00:04:02,667 --> 00:04:03,687
Brazil win a penalty,

82
00:04:03,737 --> 00:04:06,049
and with the 2024 world player of
the year on the pitch,

83
00:04:06,099 --> 00:04:07,598
Ancelotti gives the ball to Bruno.

84
00:04:07,648 --> 00:04:08,262
He misses,

85
00:04:08,312 --> 00:04:09,074
Brazil go out,

86
00:04:09,124 --> 00:04:11,620
and two days later the midfielder
writes that it hurts a lot.

87
00:04:24,235 --> 00:04:24,755
And Vinícius,

88
00:04:24,805 --> 00:04:25,786
who did not take that penalty,

89
00:04:25,836 --> 00:04:27,197
finally scores twice for
Brazil in November,

90
00:04:27,247 --> 00:04:27,795
against Japan,

91
00:04:27,845 --> 00:04:28,880
one of them into the top corner.

92
00:04:28,930 --> 00:04:30,319
Brazil still lose three-two
in stoppage time,

93
00:04:30,369 --> 00:04:32,300
for the second time in thirteen
months against the same opponent.

94
00:04:53,527 --> 00:04:55,029
And if anyone in Brazil thought the
humiliation would stay in the family,

95
00:04:55,079 --> 00:04:55,776
Argentina made sure it did not.

96
00:04:55,826 --> 00:04:56,083
In 2022,

97
00:04:56,133 --> 00:04:56,811
when Brazil go out to Croatia,

98
00:04:56,861 --> 00:04:57,845
Argentina's fans celebrate
inside the stadium.

99
00:04:57,895 --> 00:04:58,248
A year later,

100
00:04:58,298 --> 00:04:59,972
Argentina win at the Maracanã and hand Brazil
the first home defeat in the history

101
00:05:00,022 --> 00:05:00,700
of their World Cup qualifiers.

102
00:05:18,878 --> 00:05:20,975
The comparison with the past
becomes impossible to avoid.

103
00:05:21,025 --> 00:05:21,503
In 1994,

104
00:05:21,553 --> 00:05:23,220
Dunga lifts the trophy
screaming at the sky,

105
00:05:23,270 --> 00:05:25,201
and in 2002 Cafu climbs onto
the podium in Yokohama,

106
00:05:25,251 --> 00:05:26,093
with a shaved head,

107
00:05:26,143 --> 00:05:28,140
no cameras in the dressing room
and no skincare brand.

108
00:05:38,222 --> 00:05:40,971
Today's Brazil have tattoos on every arm,

109
00:05:41,021 --> 00:05:45,827
a hairdresser before every tournament and
more followers than any team on the

110
00:05:45,877 --> 00:05:46,684
planet,

111
00:05:46,734 --> 00:05:50,340
and it is tempting to conclude
that this is the problem.

112
00:05:50,773 --> 00:05:51,620
Except that in 2002,

113
00:05:51,670 --> 00:05:54,184
Ronaldo walks out with the most
ridiculous haircut in World Cup history,

114
00:05:54,234 --> 00:05:55,594
a triangle of hair on a shaved head,

115
00:05:55,644 --> 00:05:56,780
and still scores eight goals,

116
00:05:56,830 --> 00:05:57,837
two of them in the final.

117
00:05:57,887 --> 00:05:59,183
So the problem was never the hair.

118
00:05:59,233 --> 00:05:59,760
Back then,

119
00:05:59,810 --> 00:06:00,881
fame came after the trophy.

120
00:06:00,931 --> 00:06:02,740
Today it comes first, and
sometimes instead of it.

121
00:06:15,576 --> 00:06:18,542
And it is worth remembering
what is at stake.

122
00:06:18,592 --> 00:06:21,786
This is the shirt Pelé wore
at seventeen in 1958,

123
00:06:21,836 --> 00:06:24,176
the one Garrincha carried in 1962,

124
00:06:24,226 --> 00:06:28,216
the one that became the most
beautiful team in history in 1970,

125
00:06:28,266 --> 00:06:30,492
the one Romário rescued in 1994,

126
00:06:30,542 --> 00:06:32,085
and the one Ronaldo,

127
00:06:32,135 --> 00:06:35,557
Rivaldo and Ronaldinho took to
a fifth title in 2002.

128
00:06:35,607 --> 00:06:36,638
Five stars,

129
00:06:36,688 --> 00:06:39,540
and no other country in
the world has five.

130
00:06:47,667 --> 00:06:48,484
What changed is the road that leads to it.

131
00:06:48,534 --> 00:06:49,680
Brazil now export more footballers
than any country on Earth,

132
00:06:49,730 --> 00:06:50,929
one thousand four hundred and
fifty-five of them playing abroad.

133
00:06:50,979 --> 00:06:51,796
Vinícius signs for Real Madrid at sixteen,

134
00:06:51,846 --> 00:06:52,212
so does Endrick,

135
00:06:52,262 --> 00:06:52,888
and both grow up far from home,

136
00:06:52,938 --> 00:06:53,304
becoming brands,

137
00:06:53,354 --> 00:06:53,980
with sponsors and social media,

138
00:06:54,030 --> 00:06:54,917
before they become idols in
their own country.

139
00:06:54,967 --> 00:06:55,870
And the person who confirms
it is not a critic.

140
00:06:55,920 --> 00:06:56,460
It is the captain himself.

141
00:07:35,547 --> 00:07:35,960
In 2024,

142
00:07:36,010 --> 00:07:37,899
Ronaldinho had already said what
many people were thinking:

143
00:07:37,949 --> 00:07:39,201
that there was no love for the shirt,

144
00:07:39,251 --> 00:07:39,809
no fight and,

145
00:07:39,859 --> 00:07:40,330
above all,

146
00:07:40,380 --> 00:07:40,908
no football.

147
00:07:40,958 --> 00:07:41,458
Days later,

148
00:07:41,508 --> 00:07:43,339
he revealed the line was part of
an advertising campaign.

149
00:07:43,389 --> 00:07:45,220
The strange part is that almost
nobody disagreed with it.

150
00:07:55,727 --> 00:07:57,636
Through all of this,

151
00:07:57,686 --> 00:08:02,815
the national team spent twelve years
depending on a single player.

152
00:08:02,865 --> 00:08:03,934
In 2014,

153
00:08:03,984 --> 00:08:07,713
Neymar gets injured and the
seven-one follows.

154
00:08:07,763 --> 00:08:08,833
In 2022,

155
00:08:08,883 --> 00:08:12,962
he scores against Croatia and
Brazil go out anyway.

156
00:08:13,012 --> 00:08:14,362
And in 2026,

157
00:08:14,412 --> 00:08:15,971
against Norway,

158
00:08:16,021 --> 00:08:21,500
Brazil leave in the round of sixteen,
their worst World Cup since 1990.

159
00:08:32,614 --> 00:08:33,757
After Japan,

160
00:08:33,807 --> 00:08:34,712
Romário,

161
00:08:34,762 --> 00:08:36,682
a world champion in 1994,

162
00:08:36,732 --> 00:08:39,785
sums up the mood of the
country in one line:

163
00:08:39,835 --> 00:08:40,859
Ancelotti,

164
00:08:40,909 --> 00:08:42,172
that's enough.

165
00:08:42,222 --> 00:08:44,380
Pack your things and get out.

166
00:08:44,800 --> 00:08:46,208
The next World Cup is in 2030,

167
00:08:46,258 --> 00:08:46,861
in Spain,

168
00:08:46,911 --> 00:08:47,974
Portugal and Morocco.

169
00:08:48,024 --> 00:08:49,202
If Brazil do not win it,

170
00:08:49,252 --> 00:08:51,351
that will be twenty-eight
years without a title,

171
00:08:51,401 --> 00:08:53,539
and Ancelotti's contract runs
exactly until then.

172
00:08:53,589 --> 00:08:55,266
When he is asked about the criticism,

173
00:08:55,316 --> 00:08:56,340
his answer is short:

174
00:08:56,390 --> 00:08:57,300
we have a future.

175
00:09:06,363 --> 00:09:07,627
Maybe they do.

176
00:09:07,677 --> 00:09:08,582
In 2030,

177
00:09:08,632 --> 00:09:11,508
Endrick and Estêvão will be twenty-three,

178
00:09:11,558 --> 00:09:13,778
and Vinícius will turn thirty.

179
00:09:13,828 --> 00:09:16,823
But for the first time in
a very long time,

180
00:09:16,873 --> 00:09:21,660
Brazil will arrive at a World Cup without
anyone calling them favourites.

181
00:09:22,076 --> 00:09:23,186
The seven-one was supposed
to be rock bottom.

182
00:09:23,236 --> 00:09:23,777
Twelve years later,

183
00:09:23,827 --> 00:09:24,806
the best player in the world is a meme,

184
00:09:24,856 --> 00:09:25,660
the captain is asking for rest,

185
00:09:25,710 --> 00:09:26,601
and Japan have beaten Brazil twice.

186
00:09:26,651 --> 00:09:28,177
Maybe the internet's joke is closer
to the truth than it sounds,

187
00:09:28,227 --> 00:09:29,447
and something really did die
after that World Cup.

188
00:09:29,497 --> 00:09:31,220
The question is whether there is still
time to bring it back before 2030.
